### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## Requirements Analysis

**Core Functionality:**
- Generate cryptographically secure invitation tokens with configurable expiration
- Send email invitations to prospective organization members
- Assign roles to invited members upon acceptance
- Track invitation lifecycle (pending, accepted, expired, revoked)

**Security Considerations:**
- Tokens must be cryptographically random (CSPRNG), not guessable
- Tokens stored as HMAC-SHA256 hash in DB (never plaintext)
- Token expiration enforced at generation and validation time
- Rate limiting on invitation dispatch
- Single-use tokens (invalidated after acceptance)
- Inviter must have sufficient privileges
- Email enumeration protection (consistent response times)
- Organization isolation (invitations scoped to org)

**Edge Cases:**
- Re-inviting an already-pending invitee (revoke old, issue new)
- Inviting an existing member (reject)
- Expired token acceptance attempt
- Revoked token acceptance attempt
- Already-accepted token reuse
- Invalid role assignment
- Email delivery failure handling
- Concurrent acceptance race condition (DB-level uniqueness constraint)
- Inviter loses permission during invitation lifetime

**Architecture:**

```
src/
├── config/
│   └── index.ts                  # Environment configuration
├── db/
│   ├── schema.ts                 # Drizzle ORM schema definitions
│   └── client.ts                 # Database client
├── lib/
│   ├── crypto.ts                 # Token generation/hashing
│   ├── email.ts                  # Email transport abstraction
│   └── rate-limiter.ts           # In-memory + Redis rate limiting
