│   └── app.ts                    # Express application bootstrap
├── migrations/
│   ├── 001_create_organizations.sql
│   ├── 002_create_users.sql
│   ├── 003_create_invitations.sql
│   └── 004_create_memberships.sql
├── tests/
│   ├── unit/
│   │   ├── crypto/token.test.ts
│   │   ├── services/invitation.service.test.ts
│   │   └── services/email.service.test.ts
│   └── integration/
│       ├── invitation.routes.test.ts
│       └── membership.routes.test.ts
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── jest.config.ts
```

---

## Security Analysis

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Token predictability | 32-byte `crypto.randomBytes` → hex, SHA-256 HMAC with server secret |
| Token exposure in DB | Store HMAC hash, never raw token |
| Replay attacks | Single-use: token marked `used` atomically |
| Token expiry bypass | DB-level check + application-level check |
| Role escalation | Only admins/owners can invite; role ceiling enforced |
| Email enumeration | Consistent response timing; no existence disclosure |
| Concurrent redemption | Pessimistic DB row-lock during acceptance |
| CSRF on accept endpoint | Token is the auth mechanism; no session required |

---

## Edge Cases

- Invite to already-active member → reject with idempotent error
- Invite already-pending email → revoke old, issue new (configurable)
- Token expired at exact boundary → reject (non-inclusive)
- Inviter loses admin role before invite accepted → invitation remains valid (captured at issuance)
- Organization deleted → cascade-delete all pending invitations
- Invitee registers after invite issued → accept maps to existing user
- Bulk invite → rate-limited, transactional per-invite
- Maximum pending invitations per org → configurable cap

---

## Data Model

```
organizations: id, name, slug, created_at
users: id, email, password_hash, name, created_at
invitations: id, org_id, inviter_id, email, role, token_hash, status, expires_at, created_at, accepted_at, accepted_by_user_id
memberships: id, org_id, user_id, role, invited_by, created_at, updated_at
```

---

## API Surface

```
POST   /orgs/:orgId/invitations          → create invitation
GET    /orgs/:orgId/invitations          → list invitations (admin)
DELETE /orgs/:orgId/invitations/:id      → revoke invitation
POST   /invitations/accept               → accept invitation (public, token-gated)
GET    /invitations/validate/:token      → validate token (pre-flight check)
GET    /orgs/:orgId/members             → list members
DELETE /orgs/:orgId/members/:userId     → remove member
PATCH  /orgs/:orgId/members/:userId/role → update member role
```

