### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## Requirements Analysis

**Core Features:**
- Cryptographically secure invitation tokens (HMAC-SHA256 + UUID + expiry)
- Email invitation dispatching with templated emails
- Role-based assignment (Owner, Admin, Member, Viewer)
- Token lifecycle management (create, validate, accept, revoke)
- Organization membership tracking

**Security Considerations:**
- Tokens: 32-byte CSPRNG + HMAC-SHA256 signature to prevent forgery
- Token expiry: configurable TTL (default 72h)
- Single-use tokens: invalidated immediately upon acceptance
- Rate limiting on invitation creation
- Constant-time token comparison to prevent timing attacks
- Email enumeration protection (same response for valid/invalid emails)

**Edge Cases:**
- Duplicate invitations (same email + org): revoke old, issue new
- Already-a-member: reject invitation creation
- Expired tokens: cleanup via background job
- Concurrent acceptance: DB-level unique constraint + optimistic locking
- Invalid/tampered tokens: immediate rejection with audit log
- Role escalation prevention: inviter can only grant roles ≤ their own role
- Org deletion cascades to pending invitations
- Self-invitation prevention

**Architecture:**

```
src/
├── db/
│   ├── schema.ts          # Drizzle ORM schema (orgs, members, invitations)
│   └── migrations/        # SQL migrations
├── domain/
│   ├── invitation/
│   │   ├── token.ts       # Cryptographic token generation/verification
│   │   ├── service.ts     # Core invitation business logic
│   │   └── types.ts       # Domain types and enums
│   └── email/
│       ├── templates.ts   # Email HTML/text templates
│       └── dispatcher.ts  # Email sending via SMTP/SES
├── api/
│   ├── routes/
│   │   └── invitations.ts # Fastify route handlers
│   └── middleware/
│       ├── auth.ts        # JWT authentication
│       └── rateLimiter.ts # Per-user rate limiting
├── repositories/
│   ├── invitationRepo.ts  # Data access layer
│   ├── memberRepo.ts      # Member data access
│   └── orgRepo.ts         # Organization data access
├── config/
│   └── env.ts             # Validated environment config
└── tests/
    ├── token.test.ts
    ├── service.test.ts
    └── routes.test.ts
```

**Technology Stack:**
- Runtime: Node.js + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Framework: Fastify v4
- ORM: Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL
- Email: Nodemailer (SMTP/SES transport)
- Auth: JWT (jsonwebtoken)
- Validation: Zod
- Testing: Vitest
- Crypto: Node.js built-in `crypto`

